# ORDER MATTERS: for a given attribute the LAST matching line wins, so the broad default
# goes first and the specific overrides follow it. (Putting "* text=auto" last silently
# re-enabled line-ending conversion for the payload and corrupted its digests.)

# Default for the repository's own prose and config.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts keep LF whatever the platform — a CRLF script fails on Linux with the
# famously unhelpful "bash\r: command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# The payload is DATA, and its bytes are checksummed in manifest.json and in the release
# tarball's .sha256. Git must never rewrite line endings inside it: a CRLF conversion on
# checkout would silently change every digest, so a correct clone would fail its own
# integrity check. Treat the whole payload as binary.
payload/** -text
